# scripts/cfd/lib holds the OpenFOAM solve-chain SHELL library, not Python
# build output. The bare `lib/` above is packaging boilerplate and matches any
# directory named lib at ANY depth -- it silently swallowed the files that fix
# the "chain is not reproducible from a clean checkout" defect (#2023), so the
# remediation was itself invisible to git. Negation must follow the pattern it
# overrides, and the DIRECTORY must be re-included before git will descend.
!scripts/cfd/lib/

